WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.249 --> 00:00:16.190
was a public horse sale near where Mr.

2
00:00:16.230 --> 00:00:17.090
Barry had kept me.

3
00:00:18.071 --> 00:00:20.312
People came from all around to sell their horses.

4
00:00:21.612 --> 00:00:23.953
I'd never seen so many horses in one place!

5
00:00:25.014 --> 00:00:29.816
There were young horses that had never left the farm, and ponies that reminded me of Merrylegs.

6
00:00:31.676 --> 00:00:34.277
I saw hundreds of cart horses and riding horses.

7
00:00:35.398 --> 00:00:37.038
Some of the horses were quite fancy.

8
00:00:38.059 --> 00:00:43.361
Others, like me, were solid, respectable animals who had some scars but were still suitable for work.

9
00:00:44.702 --> 00:00:50.084
At the back were the sad cases—the very old, the broken down, the terribly thin.

10
00:00:51.965 --> 00:00:54.506
Only a few people wandered among those hopeless creatures.

11
00:00:55.526 --> 00:00:59.588
But the rest of the place was busy, with plenty of customers looking over the horses.

12
00:01:00.684 --> 00:01:02.485
There was bargaining going on everywhere.

13
00:01:03.466 --> 00:01:07.768
From what I heard and saw, most of it was based on lies and exaggeration.

14
00:01:09.329 --> 00:01:13.351
Mr. Barry had sent me to the sale with a horse trader who promised to sell me for

15
00:01:13.371 --> 00:01:13.991
a good price.

16
00:01:15.192 --> 00:01:20.595
I was tied beside a few other strong, useful-looking horses, and lots of people stopped to look at

17
00:01:20.675 --> 00:01:26.638
us. Well-dressed gentlemen always turned away from me as soon as they saw my scarred knees.

18
00:01:28.439 --> 00:01:30.140
But others seemed willing to overlook that.

19
00:01:31.636 --> 00:01:33.817
Most of the shoppers went through the same type of routine.

20
00:01:34.997 --> 00:01:38.238
First, they pulled open my mouth and examined my teeth to see my age.

21
00:01:39.759 --> 00:01:43.180
Then, they looked at my eyes, and felt up and down my legs and body.

22
00:01:45.280 --> 00:01:47.441
Finally, they had the seller trot me around.

23
00:01:49.061 --> 00:01:53.363
Even though the shoppers almost all did the same things, it was amazing how different it could feel,

24
00:01:53.443 --> 00:01:54.443
depending on the person.

25
00:01:55.583 --> 00:01:57.704
Some did everything in a rough, impatient way.

26
00:01:58.732 --> 00:02:02.834
They jerked my mouth open and handled my legs as if my legs were made of wood.

27
00:02:03.894 --> 00:02:07.215
Others were gentle, patting me as they went about their examination.

28
00:02:08.856 --> 00:02:10.817
One man seemed kinder than all the rest.

29
00:02:11.977 --> 00:02:14.198
I thought that if he bought me, I might be happy.

30
00:02:15.819 --> 00:02:18.280
He was a small man, but agile and quick.

31
00:02:19.520 --> 00:02:21.701
I could tell right away that he was good with horses.

32
00:02:22.822 --> 00:02:25.863
He spoke gently, and his gray eyes had a cheerful look.

33
00:02:27.043 --> 00:02:29.569
Even the scent of him was pleasing—like fresh hay.

34
00:02:31.250 --> 00:02:33.593
When he finished looking me over, he gave me a pat.

35
00:02:33.613 --> 00:02:37.496
"There's a good boy," he said.

36
00:02:38.357 --> 00:02:39.418
Then he turned to the dealer.

37
00:02:39.438 --> 00:02:42.181
"I'll give you 23 pounds for him."

38
00:02:43.722 --> 00:02:45.824
"Sorry, my friend," the dealer said.

39
00:02:45.844 --> 00:02:48.226
"This horse is worth at least thirty."

40
00:02:49.407 --> 00:02:51.369
The gray-eyed man shrugged and moved on.

41
00:02:52.110 --> 00:02:54.392
I watched him go, wishing he would come back.

42
00:02:56.744 --> 00:02:59.666
Instead a hard-faced man with a loud voice came to look at me.

43
00:03:01.307 --> 00:03:03.849
His hands were rough and careless as he checked me over.

44
00:03:04.990 --> 00:03:07.652
I was relieved when he left without saying a word to the dealer.

45
00:03:08.992 --> 00:03:11.354
I definitely didn't want to go home with a man like that!

46
00:03:12.855 --> 00:03:16.357
A few more shoppers came by, but none showed much interest in me.

47
00:03:17.258 --> 00:03:18.839
Then the hard-faced man returned.

48
00:03:20.220 --> 00:03:23.642
"23 pounds for the black horse," he told the dealer.

49
00:03:23.662 --> 00:03:25.624
"It's a fair price."

50
00:03:27.084 --> 00:03:28.085
The dealer hesitated.

51
00:03:29.626 --> 00:03:33.369
We'd been there for a while, and I guess he thought he might not get the price he

52
00:03:33.409 --> 00:03:34.090
wanted for me.

53
00:03:35.171 --> 00:03:38.914
Before he could speak, the kind, gray-eyed man came toward me again.

54
00:03:40.135 --> 00:03:43.778
I couldn't help reaching out my head toward him, and he stroked my face.

55
00:03:43.798 --> 00:03:46.620
"Hello, old boy," he told me.

56
00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:49.222
"Perhaps we're meant to be together after all."

57
00:03:50.663 --> 00:03:51.484
He looked at the dealer.

58
00:03:51.504 --> 00:03:53.205
"I'll give you 24."

59
00:03:54.486 --> 00:03:56.488
The hard-faced man shook his head and walked away.

60
00:03:58.048 --> 00:03:58.889
The dealer smiled.

61
00:03:58.909 --> 00:04:02.190
"Say 25, and he's yours," he said.

62
00:04:02.210 --> 00:04:07.033
"Twenty-four ten, and not a penny more," the gray-eyed man replied.

63
00:04:07.053 --> 00:04:09.274
"Done!" said the dealer.

64
00:04:09.294 --> 00:04:12.096
"And he's a bargain at that price, my friend.

65
00:04:13.196 --> 00:04:14.817
There's a lot of quality in this horse.

66
00:04:15.317 --> 00:04:18.039
If you want him for cab work, you won't be disappointed."

67
00:04:19.800 --> 00:04:23.962
The gray-eyed man paid for me, then took me by the halter and led me away from the

68
00:04:24.022 --> 00:04:29.637
sale. We walked to a nearby inn, where he gave me some food and water.

69
00:04:30.857 --> 00:04:34.719
A half hour later, my new owner saddled me, and we were on our way.

70
00:04:36.860 --> 00:04:39.281
We rode down pleasant country lanes and wider roads.

71
00:04:41.962 --> 00:04:44.543
The farther we went, the more crowded the roads became.

72
00:04:45.944 --> 00:04:48.925
Finally we reached a highway and rode into a bustling place.

73
00:04:51.066 --> 00:04:52.526
I'd never seen anything like it!

74
00:04:53.507 --> 00:04:58.945
There were streets to the left, streets to the right, and streets crossing one another for mile upon

75
00:04:58.985 --> 00:05:03.247
mile. Horses, carriages, and people were everywhere.

76
00:05:04.147 --> 00:05:06.928
There were new sights, new sounds, and new smells.

77
00:05:08.649 --> 00:05:12.550
It was so overwhelming that I was glad my new owner was there in the saddle to guide

78
00:05:12.590 --> 00:05:13.310
me through it all.

79
00:05:14.371 --> 00:05:16.852
We had arrived in the big city called London.
